  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nA shortwave trough moving through will continue to bring \nscattered showers this morning. Energy being advected into the \nregion behind the main troughing will allow scattered weak\nthunderstorms to develop by this afternoon. The highest CAPE\nvalues remain less than 500 J/kg and 0-6 km shear is only 10-20 \nkts, so any hail will remain small. The best chance (50-80%) for \nshowers and thunderstorms today remains from Billings east.\n\nUpper level ridging returns for Sunday through midweek, bringing\nwarm and mostly dry conditions. Highs will increase from low 70s \nto low 80s Sunday to 80s to near 90 by Wednesday. \n\nA disturbance moving across northern Montana late Sunday into \nMonday will bring widespread gusts out of the north of 25 to 40 \nmph to the region, but no precipitation is expected. Given the \nabove normal temperatures, any areas that have not recently\nreceived precip will be at a greater risk for grass fires to \nspread Monday. Take care not to cause a spark!\n\nLate week, there are signs of the pattern becoming unsettled. The\ntiming and impacts are still very uncertain, but there is moderate\nconfidence for daily precip chances to return by the end of the \nwork week. Archer",
